The CLI has some quirks, including the following.

- When adding an assignee, reporter, reviewer, or label, users are asked to select from *existing* values before they are asked to add *new* values.
  These *existing* and *new* distinctions should not exist.
  Existing values should show as the user types via tab-completion.
- All searches, lists, etc. should show the current list view.
- Checkboxes are not rendering correctly; there should not be check boxes, just checkmarks or no checkmarks.
- Query commands should have their descriptions shortened to match the description length of other commands.
